DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("cos((cos(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("sin(((x+6)^3))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((2, 9) - {-8, -5, 4})");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("((2, 9) U [1, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((2, 9))) U (2, 9)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-8, -5, 4} U [1, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-7, -4, -2, 2, 6} U {-10, -8, -5, -2, -1, 8}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-10, 3, 5, 10} U {-10, -8, -5, -2, -1, 8}) U (({-10, -8, -5, -2, -1, 8} U {-10, 3, 5, 10})) U {-10, 3, 5, 10}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`6+7+10.64+8.76`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(32.4),width=>3}
---

What is the value of [`3*15.98+12/18.68`]? [_____]{Formula('48.5823982869')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -8, -5, -2, -1, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{-7, -4, -2, 2, 6\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, 3, 5, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(C \cup A) \cup ((A \cup C)) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 2 < x < 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, -5, 4\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \geq 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`(A \cup C) \cap (A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, -9, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 6, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, -7, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, -9, -2>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, -9, -2>") x Compute("<-3, 6, -5>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, -9, -2>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 6, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -7, 2>") x Compute("<-3, 6, -5>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 1, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 5, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 1, 3>") . Compute("<-2, 5, -7>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, 5, -7>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 5, -7>") . Compute("<-9, 1, 3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 5, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>8)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
